-- A `foreign` reachable only through a core function that is itself
-- reachable only through one user call (`docs/design/backend.md` §5, §9;
-- `boundary.md` §4).
--
-- The chain is four links and every one of them is an edge of a different
-- kind:
--
--     main -> describe          (this module, a `refs` edge)
--          -> String.padLeft    (another module, an `ext_value` edge)
--          -> String.repeat     (inside core, an edge of core's own)
--          -> String.append     (a `foreign`, bound by core/String's
--                                sibling import)
--
-- **A sibling dropped one file too far is a load-time `ReferenceError`**:
-- `core/String.foreign.mjs` is copied iff one of core/String's `foreign`
-- values survived (§5), and `out/_core/String.mjs` imports the surviving
-- ones by name. Copy the file and forget the import and the name is
-- undefined; skip the copy and the import fails outright. Either way the
-- program does not start, and the build exited 0.
--
-- The output is the value, so a wrong answer fails too, not only a crash.
import Node exposing (Program)
import String


pub describe : Int → String
describe n = String.padLeft (String.fromInt n) 4 '.'


main : Program
main =
    Node.printLines
        [ describe 7
        , describe 42
        , describe 12345
        ]
